# Chthonia's workbench: the teaching layout. The editor above, and below it
# the REPL as the visible panel's first tab, with Problems, Output (a
# build's messages) and Terminal (the program Build ▸ Run starts) beside it;
# on the right the Symbols view (Chthonia's own code, chthonia.mad: the
# session's names — its functions and its variables) with the Outline as its
# second tab (View ▸ Outline shows it there) and the Markdown preview of a .md
# buffer as its third (View ▸ Markdown preview). Help ▸ Help Contents opens
# Help as a tab of the editor, beside the files (the editor pane lists the
# help view). No project tree: File ▸ Project… lists the project's files. A
# pane visible at startup whose active view is the REPL starts its session
# when the window opens (init_view_es). The editor numbers its lines and
# marks the caret line (`gutter`), as VS Code does. In a terminal the menu
# bar holds the top row (`menubar`) and the status bar the bottom one
# (`status bottom`), where the window has them.
# The same format as profiles/default.layout.
@window main
menubar
status bottom
pane editor tabs views source help focus gutter
pane sidebar right 25% tabs views symbols outline mdpreview
pane panel bottom 35% tabs views repl problems output terminal
